WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.740
- A polynomial P has zeros when
X is equal to negative four,

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.950
X is equal to three,

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.020
and X is equal to one-eighth.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.830
What could be the equation of P?

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.280
So pause this video and
think about it on your own

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.030
before we work through it together.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.140
All right.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.540
So the fact that we have
zeros at these values,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.066
that means that P of X,

00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:25.610
when X is equal to one of
these values is equal to zero.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.190
So P of negative four is equal to zero,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.560
P of three is equal to zero,

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.160
and P of one-eighth is equal to zero.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.100
And before I even look at these choices,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.450
I could think about
constructing a polynomial for

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.860
which that is true.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.910
That's going to be true if I
can express this polynomial

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.030
as the product of expressions
where each of these

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.610
would make each of those
expressions equal to zero.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.670
So what's an expression that would be zero

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.880
when X is equal to negative four?

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.420
Well the expression X plus four,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.740
this is equal to zero when
X is equal to negative four,

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.190
so I like that.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.530
What would be an expression
that would be equal to zero

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.320
when X is equal to three?

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.400
Well what about the
expression X minus three?

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.930
If X is equal to three,

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.350
then this is going to
equal to be equal zero.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.490
Zero times anything is
going to be equal to zero.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.800
So P of three would be zero in this case.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.780
And then what is an expression
that would be equal to zero

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.630
when X is equal to one-eighth?

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.930
Well that would be X minus one-eighth.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:22.763
Now tho--

00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:23.810
these aren't the only expressions.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.570
You could multiply them
by constants and still

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.500
the principles that I just
talked about would be true.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.330
But our polynomial would
look something like this.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.163
You could try it out.

00:01:32.163 --> 00:01:33.597
If X is equal to negative fou--

00:01:33.597 --> 00:01:34.430
(chuckles)

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:35.660
if X is equal to negative four,

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.330
well then this first expression is zero.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.108
Zero times something
times something is zero.

00:01:40.108 --> 00:01:42.180
Same thing for X equals three.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.370
If this right over--

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.690
If X equals three,

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.770
then X minus three is equal to zero,

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.280
and then zero times something
times something is zero.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.920
And then if X is equal to one-eighth,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.930
this expression's going
to be equal to zero.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.470
Zero times something times something

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.090
is going to be equal to zero.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.260
So which of these choices look like that?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.240
So let's see.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.280
X plus

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.160
four,

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.020
I actually see that in choices

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.110
B,

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.980
and I see that in choices D.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.670
Choice C has X minus four there.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.050
So that would have a
zero at X equals four.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.780
If X equals four, this first--

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.910
this first expression--

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.650
this first part of the expression

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.160
would be equal to zero.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.100
But we care about that happening when

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.670
X is equal to negative four.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.400
So I would actually rule out C,

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.920
and then for the same
reason I would rule out A.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.800
So we're between B and D,

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.330
and now let's see.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.190
Which of these have an
X minus three in them.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:34.630
Well I see an X minus three here.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.550
I see an X minus three there.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.730
So I like the--

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.610
I still like B and D.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.600
I'll put another check
mark right over there.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.380
And then last but not least,

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.500
which of these would be equal to zero when

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.610
X is equal to one-eighth?

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:49.550
Well, let's see.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.790
If I do one-eighth times one-eighth here

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.710
I'm gonna get one-sixty-fourth for

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.200
this part of the expression.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.510
And so that's not going
to be equal to zero.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:02:59.970
And these other two
things aren't going to be

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.130
equal to zero when X
is equal to one-eighth,

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.340
so this one is not looking so good,

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.110
but let's verify this one.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:07.410
This has--

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.460
If X is equal to one-eighth,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.530
we have eight times
one-eighth which is one,

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.500
minus one.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.930
That is going to be equal to zero,

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.970
so this one checks out.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.500
And you might be thinking hey!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.940
This last polynomial looks
a little bit different

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.760
than this polynomial that I wrote up here

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.650
when I just tried to come up
with a polynomial for which

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.350
this would be true.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.400
And as I mentioned,

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.530
you could take this and
multiply it by constants

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.600
and it would still be true.
So if you just take this,

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.800
and if we were to multiply it by eight,

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.670
you would get P of X down here,

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.330
because if we were to
multiply this times eight,

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.330
which wouldn't change the zeros,

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.030
well then if you distribute this eight,

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:47.080
this last expression would
become eight X minus one.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.243
Which is exactly what we have down here.

